==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
With a Mooth spawning alone without anything else until after 20 seconds, this becomes an extremely easy stage if you managed to kill the Mooth and use the money gained from it to deploy some more high dps rusher to rush the base (e.g., [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]). The enemy base has 187,500 HP, merely 2 hits and 500 HP away for an level 30 A. Bahamut. 20 seconds should be more than enough to deal with the first Mooth and the base in this case. Even if you failed to finish it before the 2nd enemy spawns, it's only a pitiful [[Shibalien]] with less than 15,000 HP. Don't take too much time though, as other enemies start to spawn 6.67 seconds later, which is capable of dealing some damage if you aren't paying attention.

The first Mooth has 120,000 HP with 8,400 attack. An excellent unit to rush down the Mooth is [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]], who retaliates right after every knockback, which means that it deals much more DPS in practice than the data has shown. If you don't have Butterfly Cat, you may use some other, inferior options such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] (if you have managed to beat [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]]), or even [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]]. It's much harder for non-gacha units at this point, but you may still try something like [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]], or simply just use as many Starting Money UP [[Cat Combo|Combos]] as possible (e.g., [[Crazy Hearts (Combo)|Crazed Hearts]]) and deploy A. Bahamut once you have 4500¢ in bank, but be warned, you'll have to fight through some [[Gabriel]]s and maybe [[Angelic Gory]] in this approach.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
A Similar stage as ch.1 with a tighter deployment restriction, less enemies to exploit for money, and more oppressive open.
[[Formicidaean Ariant]]is the main threat of this stage, spawning early enough before you can form a front line to KB cancel its devastating but long attack animation.
Given Formicidaean and Wild Doge are both Behemoth enemies, [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] is a good candidate to bring to dish out damage to these threats.

In some strategies, dispatching of the [[Wild Doge]]s to gun down [[Maawth]] quickly is best; to acquire some much needed cash to get ahead of the incoming storm of enemies.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
With the incredible pushing power of the Angelic Gories and Deathshund, combined with the latter's Freeze, this stage can be vicious if not prepared for correctly. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] is a must for this stage to hold ground against the Angelic Gories, alongside anti-Angel attackers like [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]. [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] should be used to keep Deathshund at bay, while units like [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] and [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Island Cat]] wear it down. Brainwashed Island's Curse can help significantly ease the difficulty of the stage by preventing Deathshund from freezing your units. In place of Brainwashed Island, [[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]] is a free unit that can also be used to curse Deathshund, though it requires the vicious [[Babies First (Merciless)|Babies First]] to be beaten. [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] is a great option for holding ground against Deathshund, though be sure not to spawn it during the Angelic Gory phases of the fight.

Alternatively, the stage can be rushed if [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]'s Explosion [[Talents|Talent]] is unlocked. With the aid of Starting Money [[Cat Combo]]s or a Rich Cat, along with cheap, fast units to act as meatshields and/or attackers in-between Bahamut's attacks (i.e. [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]]), Bahamut should clear this stage after dealing with the initial peons and timing the cat units' arrival with Deathshund's burrow. Fast and strong anti-Angel nukers, such as [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]], are also recommended to keep the Angelic Gories that spawn upon base hit at bay.

